ull},{"content_hash":"ba6545458e4c342dbbc4f44118d73ecbdcd56930c9b362db9945d956e4736fbe","event_uuid":"9286b722-9fbe-4577-93c8-c773b0ac4142","position":{"commit_sha":"278ef06184afdbf6c94bec9c7335727657fc7b15","position":"1795115893443771392-9286b722-9fbe-4577-93c8-c773b0ac4142"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9191852cd266b73bb6cf98be135af8e0723b4bf4ee73b767275b8f22e6b43c7a","event_uuid":"47c3054d-8739-4205-b7e3-ec66b08dac20","position":{"commit_sha":"ca28fad1ca439209af5b3e012e9d5a156bdbb2fb","position":"1795118383534550300-47c3054d-8739-4205-b7e3-ec66b08dac20"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0face540028427511d68410528c3cb4f442aaad8cc68b01716326bdb25d0ba14","event_uuid":"1ed0ebb8-762f-4e35-a4ac-e08c30db9688","position":{"commit_sha":"83f05e90aa5d0cf94ca8dd83b30fd1cc10c6436b","position":"1795118596216906130-1ed0ebb8-762f-4e35-a4ac-e08c30db9688"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e90962a091e8eda2a545c998578f047353fb4f7323f6102f63fe7a31e152498b","event_uuid":"00b42a48-1996-49c7-849b-f12ccbffb81a","position":{"commit_sha":"d167713866e5b1beeb6a4c26b50e888328972c44","position":"1795119026751756100-00b42a48-1996-49c7-849b-f12ccbffb81a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f5f1392ad141739f0912dee4e69d9e91b42881aa9ec302a367432e736898c2ea","event_uuid":"41e0c2d6-e5bf-4f0e-bf84-1ab3a1446d98","position":{"commit_sha":"d167713866e5b1beeb6a4c26b50e888328972c44","position":"1795119026767027047-41e0c2d6-e5bf-4f0e-bf84-1ab3a1446d98"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795115025331783185,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3167cbbc-4be9-4c71-836b-784d8a6ca754","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"977f-11fe-1dcb-4b7d"},{"link_uuid":"ccbd0d81-3c17-4745-8cb0-089158b57589","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b8dd-85be-1dbb-45b9"}],"description":"## Observation\nIn `sweep (windows)` diag run 44593555306 (throwaway branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl`, carrying the plump-smelly-indianabat, undamaging-ashamed-wasp and flowered-nonvalued-mink fixes), `test_opcert_key_copy_leak_tortoise.py::test_signer_test_modules_leave_no_key_copy_in_the_temp_dir` failed. The nested run passed. The sandbox TMPDIR it pointed at still held 13 or more `rebar-opcert-ws-*` job workspaces. 323 of the remaining files were read-only, all under `<ws>\\.git\\objects\\..`.\n\n## Cause\n`src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py::discard` removes a job workspace with `shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)`. Git writes loose objects and packs read-only. On Windows, deleting a read-only file fails with PermissionError. `ignore_errors=True` swallows that, so every op-cert job on Windows leaves its workspace (a clone of the ticket store) behind in the host temp dir. POSIX deletes read-only files when the parent dir is writable, so the leak is Windows-only.\n\n## Approach\nRewrite `workspace.discard` to call `shutil.rmtree` WITHOUT `ignore_errors` (with it set, CPython never calls the hook) and with an error hook `_retry_writable(func, path, exc)`:\n- The hook acts only when `func` is `os.unlink`, `os.remove` or `os.rmdir` (looked up at hook time); for any other failing call rmtree reports (`os.open`, `os.scandir`, `os.lstat`, `os.close`) it returns at once without retrying. For a removal it runs `os.chmod(path, stat.S_IWRITE | stat.S_IREAD)` on the path that failed, then retries `func(path)` once; any `OSError` from either step is swallowed. Adding the read bit means a directory is never left at 0o200.\n- The hook is passed as `onexc=` on Python 3.12+ and `onerror=` on 3.11 (requires-python >= 3.11), selected by `sys.version_info`.\n- The whole `rmtree` call is also wrapped in `try/except Exception`, so `discard` stays best-effort and never raises into the job (it runs in the `finally` of `jobs.py`, where an exception would replace the job's result).\n- Only the failing path is chmodded. That is enough on Windows, where the read-only attribute sits on the file and the parent dir stays deletable. On POSIX a failure would come from a parent-dir permission, which the hook does not fix, so behaviour there is unchanged apart from one extra chmod attempt after a failure.\n- The repo's other helper, `llm/workflow/snapshot.py::_rmtree_writable`, chmods the whole tree to 0o700 before removing. It is not reused, because importing `rebar.llm` into the op-cert service would pull the agents layer into a stdlib-only module.\n- Out of scope: workspaces that already leaked on Windows hosts. They are plain temp dirs named `rebar-opcert-ws-*` that the OS temp cleaner or an operator removes; no rebar data is lost.\n- No config key, env var or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py` — `discard` and its hook.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_workspace_discard_readonly.py` (new) — tests below.\n\n## Testing\nAll tests run on every platform and model Windows semantics in the test, without relying on real POSIX directory permissions:\n- A tree of writable dirs holding read-only files (mirroring `.git/objects/xx/<sha>`). `os.unlink` is patched with a fake that accepts `(path, *, dir_fd=None)`, stats the target via `os.stat(path, dir_fd=dir_fd)`, and raises `PermissionError` while the target lacks `S_IWRITE`; otherwise it calls the real `os.unlink`. `discard` removes the whole tree, and the fake saw at least one refusal.\n- `os.unlink` patched to always raise `PermissionError`: `discard` returns without raising.\n- `discard` on a path that does not exist returns without raising.\n- Calling the hook directly with `os.open` and with `os.scandir` as `func` returns without raising and without calling them again.\n- After merge: once this, plump-smelly-indianabat (which re-enables the test on Windows) and flowered-nonvalued-mink are all on main, the leak test passes in a `sweep (windows)` run on main.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `workspace.discard` removes a workspace containing read-only files on Windows semantics, proven by a test that reproduces the read-only refusal, and never raises.\n- [ ] `test_signer_test_modules_leave_no_key_copy_in_the_temp_dir` passes in a `sweep (windows)` run on main.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py","reason":"discard clears read-only bit and retries"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_workspace_discard_readonly.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b8dd-85be-1dbb-45b9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"00b42a48-1996-49c7-849b-f12ccbffb81a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability","signing"],"ticket_id":"387c-d59c-7854-40b2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: op-cert job workspaces leak in the temp dir because rmtree cannot delete read-only git objects","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f395adf1-97b3-4aa4-a1e2-27bf9f124e0b","a562d168-d0dd-4fe0-966a-fb5a62fb4dde","3167cbbc-4be9-4c71-836b-784d8a6ca754","ccbd0d81-3c17-4745-8cb0-089158b57589","9286b722-9fbe-4577-93c8-c773b0ac4142","47c3054d-8739-4205-b7e3-ec66b08dac20","1ed0ebb8-762f-4e35-a4ac-e08c30db9688","00b42a48-1996-49c7-849b-f12ccbffb81a","41e0c2d6-e5bf-4f0e-bf84-1ab3a1446d98"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795119026767027048,"uuid":"0cd97a42-4a71-4503-b80a-92cdd3762351"}